ne. The Turks conquered most of Byzantium's remaining Anatolian territories, and Andronikos spent the last years of his reign fighting his own grandson in the First Palaiologan Civil War. The war ended in Andronikos' forced abdication in 1328, after which he retired to a monastery for the remainder of his life.","wp_description":"Byzantine emperor from 1282 to 1328","wikipedia_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andronikos_II_Palaiologos","image_lead":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/54/Miniature_of_Andronikos_II.png","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Miniature_of_Andronikos_II.png/960px-Miniature_of_Andronikos_II.png","chat_ready":true,"display_from":1282,"display_to":1328}